# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# brand-growth-engine — env template (copied to ~/.hermes/.env by setup.sh)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# After setup.sh runs, this file is copied to ~/.hermes/.env (chmod 600).
# Hermes reads ~/.hermes/.env, NOT a project-local .env file.
#
# Fill in every <ANGLE_BRACKET> value. Comment out blocks you don't use yet.

# ───────── LLM provider (REQUIRED) ─────────
# Option A — Azure OpenAI via the OpenAI-compatible /openai/v1 shim (current setup):
#   Default model:  DeepSeek-V4-Flash  — the cheapest deployment on this resource,
#                   so it's the workhorse for everything (inbound replies, brand-guard,
#                   moderation). setup.sh sets it as the Hermes default automatically.
#   Escalation:     DeepSeek-V4-Pro    — stronger + pricier, same key/endpoint; only the
#                   model name changes. Used where judgment matters (voice distillation,
#                   high-visibility outbound). See HERMES_ENV.md for the per-skill policy.
#   The /openai/v1 shim handles the Azure api-version itself — no api-version needed here.
# NOTE: this is a LIVE key, committed on purpose so the repo is standalone-usable in a
# private repo. setup.sh copies this file to ~/.hermes/.env, so a fresh clone needs no
# manual key entry. If this repo ever leaks, rotate the Azure key. Full deployment
# reference (all models + keys) is in 51_AZURE_LLM_DEPLOYMENTS_AND_AGENT_RULES.md.
AZURE_FOUNDRY_API_KEY=7Q59T4x2PVt3iToAfN8d67onsv47SORtvvG0uF2SmvvxJJ4LCnHcJQQJ99BFACHYHv6XJ3w3AAAAACOGHQMr
AZURE_FOUNDRY_BASE_URL=https://072025.openai.azure.com/openai/v1
AZURE_FOUNDRY_MODEL=DeepSeek-V4-Flash

# Option B — Anthropic direct (uncomment to use instead):
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-<...>

# Option C — OpenRouter (single key, hundreds of models):
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-<...>

# ───────── X (Twitter) ─────────
# Browser path (proven): no env vars needed beyond starting the CDP Chrome.
# API path (fallback): xurl handles its own OAuth — see hermes-agent/skills/social-media/xurl/SKILL.md.
# Autonomous-cron mode requires X's explicit prior approval per Feb 2026 policy:
X_AUTO_REPLY_APPROVED=false

# ───────── LinkedIn ─────────
LI_USERNAME=<your-linkedin-email>
# Residential proxy strongly recommended for outbound (Phase 4).
# Datacenter proxies are auto-flagged. Leave commented for now.
# LI_RESIDENTIAL_PROXY_URL=http://user:pass@proxy.example.com:8080

# ───────── YouTube (Phase 1) ─────────
# YT_CHANNEL_ID=UC<...>                  # find at youtube.com/account_advanced
# YT_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=<...>.apps.googleusercontent.com
# YT_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=<...>
# After setting these:  python skills/youtube-engage/youtube_auth.py
# (writes ~/.hermes/state/youtube_token.json)

# ───────── Operations ─────────
# Time zone for schedule.yaml (IANA name).
BGE_TIMEZONE=America/Toronto
